   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing region by region. It describes a PROTAC-type molecule: a SMARCA2-binding aminopyridazine\u2013phenol unit, joined through a diazabicyclooctane, pyrimidine and cyclohexane linker to a VHL-type hydroxyproline ligand.\n\n- **Left end:** a 2-hydroxyphenyl on C3 of a pyridazine. The ring also carries an NH2 and, on the adjacent carbon, the ring nitrogen of the bicycle.\n- **Bicycle:** a 3,8-diazabicyclo[3.2.1]octane. N3 is bonded to the pyridazine and the bridging N8 is bonded to C2 of the pyrimidine.\n- **Pyrimidine and cyclohexane:** the pyrimidine is attached at C5 to a 1,4-disubstituted cyclohexane. The hashed and wedged bonds sit on opposite faces, so I treated the ring as trans.\n- **Amide chain:** the cyclohexane carbonyl is bonded to the NH of a tert-leucine. I assigned the tert-leucine as S, the hydroxyproline as (2S,4R) and the cyclohexane as trans. These come from the drawing's wedges and the standard VHL ligand pattern. I did not independently re-derive the CIP labels from the wedge geometry.\n- **Right end:** the proline C=O is bonded to an NH\u2013CH2 on a benzene ring. The ring carries an OCF3 ortho to the CH2 and a 4-methylthiazol-5-yl group para to it.\n\nI checked the trans-cyclohexane chirality tags by working out the geometry. The SMILES is valid and accounts for every atom in the drawing.\n\nSMILES: Oc1ccccc1-c1cc(N2CC3CCC(C2)N3c2ncc(cn2)[C@H]2CC[C@@H](CC2)C(=O)N[C@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N2C[C@H](O)C[C@H]2C(=O)NCc2ccc(cc2OC(F)(F)F)-c2scnc2C)c(N)nn1"
